WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:07.220
Because Brother machines pre-select needles
prior to knitting, we can check our stitch

2
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:12.580
pattern and the position of the pattern
on the needle bed. Without any yarn

3
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.940
pass the carriage to examine
the needle position.

4
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.140
In this example we'll look at the first

5
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:23.460
few rows, start with enough needles in
work to accommodate the stitch pattern

6
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.400
repeat.

7
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.700
This is stitch pattern #90
and it's a 24 stitch repeat.

8
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.360
So I've put 60 needles
into working position.

9
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.540
The pattern is set for an all-over design.

10
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:40.080
It will repeat across the needlebed.

11
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:46.020
Keep in mind that by default it will be
centered on the needle bed in this case,

12
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:52.320
needles 1 through 12,
left and right of the imaginary 0.

13
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.900
With the change knobs
set to KC (I) or KC (II)

14
00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.180
take the carriage all the way out past

15
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:04.920
the turn mark,
then pass the carriage across the needles.

16
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.740
I've double-checked and it's these needles

17
00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.180
that we'll be for the heel of the boot
and they've been selected.

18
00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:18.960
Needles number 5 through 11
and there are repeats across the bed.

19
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.850
Pass the carriage back for row 2

20
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:30.540
and confirm that these needles
are selected. On row 3

21
00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.960
Again, read your pattern and you should

22
00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.540
be able to see that these
needles are selected.

23
00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.820
Can you see the value in dry knitting?
No

24
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.740
guesswork. You know where the patterning is

25
00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:45.640
going to occur even before
threading up the machine.

